- # `↯/s.34.1` — `Regex.Error`
+ # `↯/s.34.1` — `Regex.Error`

- Raised when Kaleidoscope cannot parse a regular expression literal.
- Each variant pinpoints the syntactic problem.
+ Levée lorsque Kaleidoscope ne parvient pas à analyser un littéral d'expression régulière.
+ Chaque variante désigne précisément le problème syntaxique.

- ## Cause
+ ## Cause

- The `r"…"` regex interpolator parses the pattern at compile time. When
- the parser cannot accept the input, it throws a `Regex.Error` carrying
- the character `index` at which the problem was detected and a `Reason`
- explaining what was expected. The constructed message is `the regular
+ L'interpolateur de regex `r"…"` analyse le motif à la compilation. Lorsque
+ l'analyseur ne peut pas accepter l'entrée, il lance une `Regex.Error` portant
+ l'`index` du caractère auquel le problème a été détecté et une `Reason`
+ expliquant ce qui était attendu. Le message construit est `the regular

- expression could not be parsed because $reason at $index`.
+ expression could not be parsed because $reason at $index`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Code
+ column  Code

- column  Reason
- column  Meaning
+ column  Raison
+ column  Signification

- column  Message
+ column  Message

- column  Resolution
- row  `↯/s.34.1.1`  `UnclosedGroup`  A capturing group was opened with `(` but never closed with `)`.  `[↯/s.34.1.1] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group was not closed at 11`  Add the missing `)` or escape the `(` if a literal parenthesis is intended.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.2`  `ExpectedGroup`  An extractor pattern was used in a context that requires a capturing group to follow it, but no group was found.  `[↯/s.34.1.2] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group was expected immediately following an extractor at 0`  Wrap the extracted portion of the pattern in `(…)`.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.3`  `BadRepetition`  A repetition range `{n,m}` has `m < n`.  `[↯/s.34.1.3] the regular expression could not be parsed because the maximum number of repetitions is less than the minimum at 5`  Swap the bounds, or use `{n,}` if no upper bound is needed.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.4`  `Uncapturable`  A capturing group is nested inside a repeating group, which means it cannot be extracted unambiguously.  `[↯/s.34.1.4] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group inside a repeating group can not be extracted at 7`  Either remove the capture by switching to a non-capturing group `(?:…)`, or restructure the pattern so the repetition is inside the capture rather than outside it.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.5`  `UnexpectedChar`  A character that does not belong in a repetition range was encountered.  `[↯/s.34.1.5] the regular expression could not be parsed because the repetition range contained an unexpected character at 9`  Use only digits and a single comma between `{` and `}`.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.6`  `NotInGroup`  A `)` was encountered with no corresponding `(`.  `[↯/s.34.1.6] the regular expression could not be parsed because a closing parenthesis was found without a corresponding opening parenthesis at 4`  Add the missing `(`, escape the `)` if it should be literal, or remove the stray closing parenthesis.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.7`  `IncompleteRepetition`  A repetition range was opened with `{` but never closed with `}`.  `[↯/s.34.1.7] the regular expression could not be parsed because the repetition range was not closed at 8`  Add the missing `}`.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.8`  `InvalidPattern`  The pattern was rejected by the underlying parser for a reason that does not fit any of the more specific variants.  `[↯/s.34.1.8] the regular expression could not be parsed because the pattern was invalid at 3`  Review the pattern around the reported index; consult the regex syntax for the construct in use.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.9`  `UnclosedEscape`  The pattern ends with a `\` that has nothing to escape.  `` [↯/s.34.1.9] the regular expression could not be parsed because nothing followed the escape character `\` at 12 ``  Either remove the trailing backslash or escape the character that should follow it.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.10`  `EmptyCharClass`  A character class `[…]` contained no characters.  `[↯/s.34.1.10] the regular expression could not be parsed because the character class is empty at 2`  Add at least one character to the class, or remove the empty `[]`.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.11`  `ZeroMaximum`  A repetition range had a maximum of zero, e.g. `{0,0}` or `{0}`.  `[↯/s.34.1.11] the regular expression could not be parsed because the maximum number of repetitions must be greater than zero at 6`  Use a maximum greater than zero, or remove the repeated subpattern entirely if it should never match.
+ column  Résolution
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.1`  `UnclosedGroup`  Un groupe capturant a été ouvert avec `(` mais jamais fermé avec `)`.  `[↯/s.34.1.1] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group was not closed at 11`  Ajoutez la `)` manquante, ou échappez la `(` si une parenthèse littérale est voulue.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.2`  `ExpectedGroup`  Un motif d'extracteur a été utilisé dans un contexte qui exige qu'un groupe capturant le suive, mais aucun groupe n'a été trouvé.  `[↯/s.34.1.2] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group was expected immediately following an extractor at 0`  Entourez de `(…)` la partie extraite du motif.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.3`  `BadRepetition`  Un intervalle de répétition `{n,m}` a `m < n`.  `[↯/s.34.1.3] the regular expression could not be parsed because the maximum number of repetitions is less than the minimum at 5`  Inversez les bornes, ou utilisez `{n,}` si aucune borne supérieure n'est nécessaire.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.4`  `Uncapturable`  Un groupe capturant est imbriqué dans un groupe répété, ce qui signifie qu'il ne peut pas être extrait sans ambiguïté.  `[↯/s.34.1.4] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group inside a repeating group can not be extracted at 7`  Supprimez la capture en passant à un groupe non capturant `(?:…)`, ou restructurez le motif pour que la répétition soit à l'intérieur de la capture plutôt qu'à l'extérieur.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.5`  `UnexpectedChar`  Un caractère qui n'a pas sa place dans un intervalle de répétition a été rencontré.  `[↯/s.34.1.5] the regular expression could not be parsed because the repetition range contained an unexpected character at 9`  N'utilisez que des chiffres et une seule virgule entre `{` et `}`.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.6`  `NotInGroup`  Une `)` a été rencontrée sans `(` correspondante.  `[↯/s.34.1.6] the regular expression could not be parsed because a closing parenthesis was found without a corresponding opening parenthesis at 4`  Ajoutez la `(` manquante, échappez la `)` si elle doit être littérale, ou supprimez la parenthèse fermante superflue.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.7`  `IncompleteRepetition`  Un intervalle de répétition a été ouvert avec `{` mais jamais fermé avec `}`.  `[↯/s.34.1.7] the regular expression could not be parsed because the repetition range was not closed at 8`  Ajoutez l'accolade `}` manquante.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.8`  `InvalidPattern`  Le motif a été rejeté par l'analyseur sous-jacent pour une raison qui ne correspond à aucune des variantes plus spécifiques.  `[↯/s.34.1.8] the regular expression could not be parsed because the pattern was invalid at 3`  Examinez le motif autour de l'indice signalé ; consultez la syntaxe des regex pour la construction utilisée.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.9`  `UnclosedEscape`  Le motif se termine par un `\` qui n'a rien à échapper.  `` [↯/s.34.1.9] the regular expression could not be parsed because nothing followed the escape character `\` at 12 ``  Supprimez la barre oblique inverse finale, ou échappez le caractère qui doit la suivre.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.10`  `EmptyCharClass`  Une classe de caractères `[…]` ne contenait aucun caractère.  `[↯/s.34.1.10] the regular expression could not be parsed because the character class is empty at 2`  Ajoutez au moins un caractère à la classe, ou supprimez le `[]` vide.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.11`  `ZeroMaximum`  Un intervalle de répétition avait un maximum de zéro, par exemple `{0,0}` ou `{0}`.  `[↯/s.34.1.11] the regular expression could not be parsed because the maximum number of repetitions must be greater than zero at 6`  Utilisez un maximum supérieur à zéro, ou supprimez entièrement le sous-motif répété s'il ne doit jamais correspondre.

